# The demonstration (roadmap l4.md L11, D19), as `make run` shows it: the
# clock writes the time on the status line every second and the counter
# says how fast it counts, which is how much of the CPU nothing else wants,
# while the shell runs commands. In TEST_DEMO builds the OS server puts
# their status lines on the log too, where the runner sets them apart
# ("status, NAME: TEXT", after the line each fell in: the clock's report of
# its fault ends the first), and the clock faults once, after three
# seconds: the OS server reports it and starts it again while the shell
# works on.
# ps lists every module the root built; kill stops the clock, which shows
# no more: everything made for it is revoked and its memory given back
# (roadmap l4.md L12); start builds it again from that memory, its data
# afresh from the module, so it faults once more; neither touches anything
# but a background program. The clock, above the shell, ticks on while the shell
# spins, until Ctrl+Break; the counter, below it, does not count then.
program: shell
define: TEST_DEMO
keys: {wait 250}ps\nkill clock\n{wait 100}ps\nstart clock\n{wait 250}kill program\nkill nothing\nstart counter\nkill\nspin\n{wait 150}{ctrl-break}\n
timeout: 120
match: contains
---
rx286 shell: type help for the commands
rx286: clock fault #UD at 0007:{l:entry.fault}
status, clock:
status, counter: idle
status, clock:
  # name     kind       priority state, runs
  0 root     root       7        running,
  1 os       OS server  5        awaiting a notification,
  2 printer  driver     6        receiving,
  6 fd       driver     6        receiving,
  9 sound    driver     6        receiving,
 10 rtc      driver     6        receiving,
 11 program  foreground 3        awaiting its reply,
 12 clock    background 4
 13 counter  background 1
A:\>kill clock
A:\>ps
 12 clock    background 4        stopped,
A:\>start clock
rx286: clock fault #UD at 0007:{l:entry.fault}
status, clock:
kill program
Not a background program
A:\>kill nothing
No such program
A:\>start counter
It is running already
A:\>kill
Required parameter missing
A:\>spin
rx286: Ctrl+Break: the program starts again
status, clock:
rx286 shell, started again
